// DandysWorldToonsMaker Accessory files
// Comment below

Line 1: Accessory name (optional)
Line 2: Accessory's x-file
Line 3: Scaling level
Line 4: Position (x, y, z)
Line 5: Rotation angle (x, y, z)
Line 6: Bone name (the accessory follows the movement of this bone)

Accessories are standard .x files.
You can create your own accessories using Metasequoia or something similar.
DandysWorldToonsMaker Then, load the accessory and try setting the scaling, position, and rotation angle through trial and error.
